WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.920
"American Horror Story" is never a show&nbsp;
that shies away from the potential for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.560
controversy. From its inception in 2011,&nbsp;
the FX horror anthology has consistently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.920
pushed the envelope and forced viewers&nbsp;
to confront some of their deepest fears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.680
While "Coven" is typically regarded as one&nbsp;
of the most beloved seasons of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.600
it was still full of many moments that forced&nbsp;
fans to stop and consider what they were watching.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.120
The witchy third season indulges&nbsp;
in campiness alongside the horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.520
but also included many genuinely uncomfortable&nbsp;
moments that made fans squirm in their seats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.840
for all the wrong reasons. There were plenty&nbsp;
of not safe for work scenes that got to fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.840
especially because many of them veered heavily&nbsp;
into lurid and exploitative imagery. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.240
also several graphic torture scenes, where&nbsp;
people lost body parts in terrifying ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.720
"Coven" stood out just as much for its&nbsp;
occult themes as it did for gory scenes.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.680
On the show's subreddit, one user&nbsp;
asked fans to share what scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.720
they found the scariest. One fan&nbsp;
jokingly called the show "American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Trauma Story'' after scrolling through&nbsp;
all of the frightening scenes. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.760
one scene from "Coven'' came up multiple&nbsp;
times and stood out among the various answers.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.640
We actually wonder how Reddit&nbsp;
managed to narrow it down to just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.560
one that went too far. The mere idea of&nbsp;
Madame Delphine, played by Kathy Bates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.400
systematically removing the toes of a gardener&nbsp;
who had the audacity to come looking for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.120
bandage makes our hairs stand on end. There's&nbsp;
also the self-imposed punishment of Cordelia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.600
where she decides that she can only gain The Sight&nbsp;
by destroying her own eyes with a set of garden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.480
shears. If nothing else, it's a great excuse to&nbsp;
never do any work outside in the near future.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.520
"My blindness gave me real vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.320
but it's of no use to me now. Not when there&nbsp;
are witch hunters right outside our door."

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.720
While we're on the subject of eyes, we can't&nbsp;
forget about the big murder moment for Myrtle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.560
The next time you get a craving for fresh fruit,&nbsp;
try not to think about the time she scooped out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.640
the eyes from the sockets of Quentin and Pemby.&nbsp;
It's bad enough that she extracts these from her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.160
two victims while they're still alive, but&nbsp;
she took it a step further. Thanks to one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.160
of her concoctions, Cecily and Quentin are&nbsp;
completely immobilized during this impromptu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.640
surgery. They can still feel every agonizing&nbsp;
moment while Myrtle revels in her revenge.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.480
We could spend hours dissecting the brutal&nbsp;
moments throughout "AHS: Coven" that make us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.400
want to reconsider ever attending a dinner&nbsp;
party involving cocktails with garnishes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.440
but there's only one that will&nbsp;
haunt us until the end of our days.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.680
In keeping with many fan criticisms of "Coven"&nbsp;
that have popped up in retrospectives of "American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.680
Horror Story," several Redditors pointed to the&nbsp;
opening scene of the season premiere as being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.680
particularly difficult to watch, although&nbsp;
we would say that's putting it mildly. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.560
episode opens with real-life serial killer Madame&nbsp;
Delphine LaLaurie hosting a party in New Orleans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.320
where she is punishing one of her daughters&nbsp;
for trying to seduce a Black houseman. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.000
truly sadistic fashion, he's the one who&nbsp;
bears the brunt of the punishment. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.840
follows is one of the most horrifying&nbsp;
sequences in the history of "AHS,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.000
transcending the horror genre and hitting even&nbsp;
closer to home in today's cultural climate.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.480
The sadistic socialite brings the man, Bastien, to&nbsp;
the attic, where it's revealed that she keeps many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.720
others in a makeshift torture chamber. Delphine&nbsp;
cruelly mocks her abused captives, calling them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.200
her pets as they watch in horror while Bastien's&nbsp;
head is covered by a hollowed-out bull's head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.000
He whimpers while she says he's to become a beast,&nbsp;
since he acted like one, citing her inspiration as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.880
the mythological Greek minotaur. The head is then&nbsp;
bonded to his body, completing the transformation.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.120
Fans agreed that the brutal, grotesque scene&nbsp;
went too far, with users claiming they almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.120
gave up on the rest of the season due to this&nbsp;
opener. Despite staying on the air for a decade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.640
it makes us wonder how many potential&nbsp;
"American Horror Story" fans have checked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.680
out thanks to the plethora of shocking&nbsp;
moments throughout the show's history.

